Container orchestration is the process of managing multiple containers automatically, including deployment, scaling, and monitoring. While Docker is used to run containers, orchestration tools like Kubernetes manage them at scale. They ensure high availability, auto-scaling, and self-healing by restarting failed containers and balancing traffic. In DevOps, container orchestration is important because it enables efficient and reliable production deployments. 

 

