7. How do you optimize Docker image size? 

Use Alpine or minimal base images (e.g., node:16-alpine instead of node:16) 

Use multi-stage builds to exclude build dependencies from the final image 

Remove unnecessary files, caches, and temp files in the same RUN layer 

Use .dockerignore to exclude node_modules, .git, logs, etc. 

Combine multiple RUN commands using && to reduce layer count 

👉 Real-time benefit: Reduced image size speeds up pull times and deployment. 

 

8. What are multi-stage Docker builds? 

Multi-stage builds split the build and runtime environments into separate stages. Only the required artifacts are copied to the final image, eliminating build tools and reducing image size significantly. 

Example (Java App): 

# Stage 1: Build 

FROM maven:3.8 AS build 

WORKDIR /app 

COPY . . 

RUN mvn package -DskipTests 

 

# Stage 2: Runtime only 

FROM openjdk:17-jre-slim 

COPY --from=build /app/target/app.jar app.jar 

ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"] 

👉 Only final artifacts are included — no Maven, no source code in the runtime image. 

 

