20. What are best practices for Docker in production? 

Use lightweight, minimal base images (Alpine, distroless) 

Avoid running containers as root — use non-root USER in Dockerfile 

Apply semantic versioning for image tags — never use 'latest' in production 

Enable centralized logging and monitoring (Prometheus, ELK) 

Use container orchestration tools like Kubernetes for scaling and self-healing 

Keep containers stateless — store state externally (DB, volumes, cache) 

Regularly scan images for security vulnerabilities (Trivy, Snyk) 

Use health checks (HEALTHCHECK in Dockerfile, liveness/readiness probes in K8s) 

Maintain immutable infrastructure — rebuild, don't patch running containers 

Set resource limits (CPU and memory) on all containers 

 

